@tradition name-on-the-beam-new
// Name on the beam for a new Works hand (0.70.0, playtest 1: the user, "you on arrival, and each new Works member
// later"; the traditions engineer). The Monday after a crew rotation brings someone new to Works (when: rotation monday
// dept works; ROSTER_ROTATIONS: days 35, 77, 161 so far), straight from shift: the Works crew gather under the bay's cross
// beam and the newcomer paints their first name beside everyone else's. Same places as yours (the deck architect's
// 5-beam-1..8, pool @name-beam). You just turn up (no tap): their name goes on the beam (section 18's beamNames).
// Placeholder words by the traditions engineer until the head writer's.
k: 485
title: Name on the beam
when: rotation monday dept works
at: 17:05-17:40
min: 15
prio: 2
after-shift: yes
venue: works-bay
where: 5 pool @name-beam
where: 5 room Tea corner: lounge-seat
hold: none
who: honoree always, calder always, torres-zeke always, pell 95%, works 80%
anim: talk
host: torres-zeke
from: calder


== mail
- {names} joined Works on Sunday's shuttle. After shift tomorrow, stay in the bay: their name goes on the beam.

== ask
- Stay after shift. {first}'s name goes on the beam tonight.
- New hand on the beam at five. Don't run off.

== here
- Big letters, {first}. Make it last.   #warm
- Welcome to Works, {first}.   #warm
- There's room up there yet. Just about.   #funny

== thanks
- Under the cross beam, the Works crew gather round while {first} paints their name beside all the others. Everyone cheers.   #warm

== chatter
- New hand's name goes on the beam tonight.
- Another name on the beam. It's getting crowded up there.   #funny
